🎗️ 29.14 Why wait()?

👉 Suppose:

zeroFlag = false
The Zero Thread enters.
It is not its turn.

Therefore:

while (!zeroFlag) {
    wait();
}

The thread:

🔴 enters WAITING state
🔴 releases the monitor
🔴 allows the other thread to execute

🎗️ 29.15 Why while Instead of if?

👉 Wrong

if (!zeroFlag) {
    wait();
}

👉 Correct

while (!zeroFlag) {
    wait();
}

After waking up, the thread must re-check the condition.

👉 Reasons:
🔴 Spurious wakeups
🔴 Another thread may change the state
🔴 Multiple threads may be waiting in more complex versions

Therefore:

wait()
  ↓
Wake up
  ↓
Re-check condition
  ↓
Can I proceed?
  ↓
Yes → Continue
No  → wait() again

🎗️ 29.16 Why notifyAll()?

After Zero prints:

zeroFlag = !zeroFlag;
notifyAll();

The Even-Odd Thread needs to wake up.

Similarly, after Even-Odd prints:

zeroFlag = !zeroFlag;
notifyAll();

the Zero Thread needs to wake up.

Therefore:

Zero prints
   ↓
zeroFlag = false
   ↓
notifyAll()
   ↓
Even-Odd wakes


Even-Odd prints
   ↓
zeroFlag = true
   ↓
notifyAll()
   ↓
Zero wakes

🎗️ 29.17 Why zeroFlag = !zeroFlag?

Instead of writing:

zeroFlag = false;

and:

zeroFlag = true;

we can simply toggle it:

zeroFlag = !zeroFlag;

The states alternate:

true
 ↓
false
 ↓
true
 ↓
false
 ↓
true

Therefore:

true  → Zero Thread
false → Even-Odd Thread
🎗️ 29.18 Important Point — Who Increments the Number?

Only the Even-Odd Thread increments the number.

currNumber++;

The Zero Thread never increments it.

Why?

Zero is only a separator.

Its responsibility is:

Print 0
   ↓
Transfer control

The Even-Odd Thread owns the actual number sequence:

1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5
🎗️ 29.19 Implement printZero()
public synchronized void printZero()
        throws InterruptedException {


    while (currNumber <= limit) {


        while (!zeroFlag) {
            wait();
        }


        if (currNumber > limit) {
            break;
        }


        System.out.println(
                Thread.currentThread().getName()
                        + " : " + 0
        );


        zeroFlag = !zeroFlag;


        notifyAll();
    }
}
