🎗️ 29.30 Why Doesn't the Even-Odd Thread Need Separate Odd and Even Logic?

Because this implementation does not have separate Odd and Even threads.

The same thread:

Even-Odd-Thread

prints:

1
2
3
4
5
...

It doesn't need to check:

currNumber % 2

because its only responsibility is:

Print the current number whenever zeroFlag == false.

Therefore, the pattern automatically becomes:

0 1
0 2
0 3
0 4
...
